    "done_when": "At the node's base, tests/test_server_listens_before_it_watches.py and tests/test_tag_inventory.py are run together in one process with -p no:xdist, in both file orders, three times each. Each run logs whether tests/test_tag_inventory.py::test_discovery_derives_tag_inventory_from_every_resource_type failed, and the value of reckon.serve._SIGNATURE_TTL_S once the server tests' fixtures have torn down. The manifest names the mechanism at file and line. It names which write to _SIGNATURE_TTL_S can survive the served_entry_point fixture's teardown (serve.main sets it at reckon/serve.py:3397 to :3399 on the daemon thread), and why the fixture's monkeypatch undo does not cover that write. The fix keeps the served thread's configuration inside its own test. The fixture does not return from teardown until the served thread has stopped, and it restores the memo only after the thread's last write. A teardown check then fails the server test if serve._SIGNATURE_TTL_S is not 0.0. After the fix, the pair passes in one process in both orders, five of five each. The declared negative control is executed and logged: in a scratch tree, drop the fix so the served thread writes the memo after teardown, and the teardown check fails the server test. If the base runs do not reproduce the failure, the manifest says so, and the fix and its control still land. No assertion is deleted. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and literal command, and ends EXIT=, and basetemps under /tmp are deleted afterwards. Only tests/test_server_listens_before_it_watches.py changes. If the write cannot be contained without a change to reckon/serve.py, the manifest reports status blocked and names that change, and no other file is edited.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
